#: envinsp_settings.py:207
msgid ""
"A colon-separated list of interface languages, tried in order, for example "
"LANGUAGE=de:en. It overrides LANG and LC_MESSAGES for the interface "
"language. Set it in a terminal (LANGUAGE=de gramps) or in the Exec line of "
"the Gramps desktop launcher."
msgstr ""

#: envinsp_settings.py:213
msgid ""
"The default locale for every category that is not set on its own. Normally "
"set by the desktop from its language and region settings."
msgstr ""

#: envinsp_settings.py:217
msgid ""
"Overrides LANG and every LC_ variable at once. Usually left unset; set it "
"only for testing, for example LC_ALL=fr_FR.UTF-8 gramps."
msgstr ""

#: envinsp_settings.py:220
msgid "The locale for interface text, when LANGUAGE is not set."
msgstr ""

#: envinsp_settings.py:221
msgid "The locale for dates and times (month and day names)."
msgstr ""

#: envinsp_settings.py:222
msgid "The locale for sorting."
msgstr ""

#: envinsp_settings.py:223
msgid "The locale for numbers (decimal separator)."
msgstr ""

#: envinsp_settings.py:224
msgid "The locale for currency amounts."
msgstr ""

#: envinsp_settings.py:226
msgid ""
"Read by Gramps itself, only with PyICU installed: an ICU locale for sorting "
"that overrides LC_COLLATE, for example COLLATION=sv. It can also choose a "
"special sort order, such as the German phone book order: "
"COLLATION=de_DE@collation=phonebook."
msgstr ""

#: envinsp_settings.py:233
msgid ""
"Environment variables are read once, when Gramps starts. Set them in a "
"terminal before the gramps command, in the desktop launcher, or (on Windows) "
"in the system environment variables."
msgstr ""

#: envinsp_settings.py:242
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Normally set by the desktop region or formats settings. Overridden by the "
"%(var)s environment variable, or by LC_ALL; when neither is set, LANG "
"decides."
msgstr ""

